{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pulls/6","id":5154757998,"node_id":"PR_kwDOMu9dys8AAAABMz9dbg","html_url":"https://github.com/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pull/6","diff_url":"https://github.com/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pull/6.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pull/6.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/issues/6","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pulls/6/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pulls/6/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/issues/6/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dfki-ric/uxo-dataset2024/statuses/8810df836c8391dd5cea9c6824093e988c46c8dd","number":6,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Rerun visualization","user":{"login":"olayasturias","id":16150429,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTUwNDI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16150429?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias","html_url":"https://github.com/olayasturias","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nAdds `rerun_viz/log_to_rerun.py`, which logs exported recordings to [Rerun](https://rerun.io). The GoPro, ARIS and gantry data can then be scrubbed together in one synchronized 3D scene.\n\nFor each recording it shows:\n\n- **3D scene:** the gantry → AR3 → sonar/camera pose chain, built from `calibration/transforms.yaml`, `gantry.csv` and the AR3 pan/tilt/roll in `aris_frame_meta.csv`. This is the same composition as `_create_ar3_df` in `release_1_export.py`. The scene also includes the full AR3 trajectory, the target pose, the GoPro camera frustum, the ARIS field of view as a frustum, and the ARIS returns back-projected into 3D.\n- **GoPro:** each frame with its bounding-box label (×3), the ARIS field-of-view outline, and the ARIS returns projected into the image.\n- **ARIS polar** images, **time series** of gantry position and AR3 pan/tilt/roll, the target's **textured 3D scan**, and the recording **notes**.\n- Two timelines: `aris_frame` and `time` (ARIS timestamp).\n\nThe ARIS does not resolve elevation, so the image overlay has two modes (`--overlay-mode`):\n\n- `band` (default): each return is spread over the vertical aperture as a heatmap, weighted by the beam pattern (half strength at the edges).\n- `line`: each return is drawn as a point at zero elevation.\n\n## Other changes\n\n- **README:** new \"Visualizing the data in Rerun\" section covering install, downloading the 1.7 GB Zenodo sample, usage, options and limitations.\n- **`requirements.txt`:** adds `rerun-sdk==0.41.0`, `opencv-python-headless==4.10.0.84` and `py7zr==0.22.0`. OpenCV was already used by `view_recording.py` but was not listed. The headless build avoids Qt conflicts with PyQt5.\n- **`.gitignore`:** ignores `data_download/` and `.venv*`. It also adds the missing newline at the end of the file.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Logged all five recordings in the Zenodo `sample.7z` and inspected them in the Rerun viewer.\n- Pose chain check on the left-to-right sweeps: the target projects into the labelled GoPro boxes and lies inside the ARIS range window.\n- Fresh Python 3.12 environment installed from `requirements.txt` (NumPy 2.0.1, OpenCV 4.10, pandas 2.2.2); ran the script in both overlay modes.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- The 14° vertical aperture is the ARIS Explorer 3000 specification, not a value from the data. It can be changed with `--sonar-elevation`.\n- The left/right sign of the ARIS beams follows `prep_2_aris_to_polar.py` and has not been verified independently. The target stays near the centre of the beam, so the effect is small.\n- GoPro frames use the `linear` intrinsics without undistortion.\n- Camera-to-target alignment is looser in the flyby recordings than in the left-to-right sweeps.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-04T13:05:46Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T13:05:46Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"be2bd53a4d7ec510527d28ac426f58c1d3a1af61","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"olayasturias:rerun-visualization","ref":"rerun-visualization","repo":{"id":1445658283,"node_id":"R_kgDOVir-qw","name":"uxo-dataset2024","full_name":"olayasturias/uxo-dataset2024","owner":{"login":"olayasturias","id":16150429,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTUwNDI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16150429?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias","html_url":"https://github.com/olayasturias","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olayasturias/repos","events_url":"https://api.githu